","\u002Finternals\u002Fwolf","7.internals\u002F6.wolf",{"id":213,"title":191,"body":214,"description":1668,"extension":1669,"links":1670,"meta":1671,"navigation":1672,"path":192,"seo":1673,"stem":193,"__hash__":1674},"docs_en\u002F7.internals\u002F2.apps.md",{"type":215,"value":216,"toc":1656},"minimark",[217,227,232,249,254,422,429,434,575,581,595,598,605,686,732,818,825,831,835,838,888,923,938,941,944,967,978,1057,1073,1093,1098,1102,1113,1180,1211,1244,1250,1312,1326,1341,1344,1354,1359,1442,1447,1548,1554,1559,1563],[218,219,220,221,226],"p",{},"Read from the commits listed in ",[222,223,225],"a",{"href":224},"\u002Finternals#what-was-read","the overview",". Paths are relative to each repository.",[228,229,231],"h2",{"id":230},"central","Central",[218,233,234,235,239,240,244,245,248],{},"One Frappe 16 app and a Vue console (",[236,237,238],"code",{},"\u002Fdashboard",") on ",[241,242,243],"strong",{},"one global site",". It owns identity, teams, capabilities, the catalogue, billing, the list of regions and the managed services. It reaches a region only through ",[236,246,247],{},"central\u002Fintegrations\u002F",".",[218,250,251],{},[241,252,253],{},"Stores.",[255,256,257,270],"table",{},[258,259,260],"thead",{},[261,262,263,267],"tr",{},[264,265,266],"th",{},"Purpose",[264,268,269],{},"DocTypes",[271,272,273,307,318,332,362,377,404],"tbody",{},[261,274,275,279],{},[276,277,278],"td",{},"Teams and rights",[276,280,281,284,285,288,289,292,293,292,296,299,300,302,303,306],{},[236,282,283],{},"Team"," (with an immutable 32-bit ",[236,286,287],{},"tenant_id","; 0 is reserved for the platform), ",[236,290,291],{},"Team Member",", ",[236,294,295],{},"Team Role",[236,297,298],{},"Capability"," (18, on two planes: ",[236,301,230],{}," and ",[236,304,305],{},"atlas",")",[261,308,309,312],{},[276,310,311],{},"Regions",[276,313,314,317],{},[236,315,316],{},"Region",": the Atlas address, the proxy domain, one webhook secret for Atlas and one for Cargo, the telemetry data source",[261,319,320,323],{},[276,321,322],{},"Keys",[276,324,325,328,329,306],{},[236,326,327],{},"Central SSO Settings",": three signing keys (see ",[222,330,196],{"href":331},"\u002Finternals\u002Finterop#keys",[261,333,334,337],{},[276,335,336],{},"Servers",[276,338,339,342,343,346,347,292,350,292,353,292,356,292,359],{},[236,340,341],{},"Virtual Machine"," (Central's record of a server), ",[236,344,345],{},"Resource Action"," (one row per create, start, stop, resize, terminate), ",[236,348,349],{},"Pilot Credential",[236,351,352],{},"VM Snapshot",[236,354,355],{},"Team SSH Key",[236,357,358],{},"Firewall Ruleset",[236,360,361],{},"WireGuard Device",[261,363,364,367],{},[276,365,366],{},"Sites and routes",[276,368,369,372,373,376],{},[236,370,371],{},"Site"," (only the site baked into a trial image), ",[236,374,375],{},"Site Domain"," (one proxy route per hostname)",[261,378,379,382],{},[276,380,381],{},"Billing",[276,383,384,385,292,388,292,391,292,394,292,397,292,400,403],{},"About 55 DocTypes: ",[236,386,387],{},"Plan",[236,389,390],{},"Subscription",[236,392,393],{},"Invoice",[236,395,396],{},"Usage Day",[236,398,399],{},"Usage Rollup",[236,401,402],{},"Credit Wallet","…",[261,405,406,409],{},[276,407,408],{},"Feed",[276,410,411,414,415,418,419],{},[236,412,413],{},"Activity Event"," (kept 365 days), ",[236,416,417],{},"Team Notification",", 49 ",[236,420,421],{},"Notification Event Type",[218,423,424,425,428],{},"There is ",[241,426,427],{},"no Bench DocType and no deployment record",". What a server runs is Pilot's business.",[218,430,431],{},[241,432,433],{},"Accepts.",[255,435,436,449],{},[258,437,438],{},[261,439,440,443,446],{},[264,441,442],{},"From",[264,444,445],{},"Entry",[264,447,448],{},"Authenticated by",[271,450,451,465,495,517,530,549,564],{},[261,452,453,456,462],{},[276,454,455],{},"A person",[276,457,458,459],{},"The console and ",[236,460,461],{},"central.api.{servers,sites,snapshots,teams,ssh_keys,wireguard,firewall_rulesets,activity,…}",[276,463,464],{},"A Frappe session, then a capability",[261,466,467,470,488],{},[276,468,469],{},"Pilot",[276,471,472,292,475,478,479,292,482,292,485],{},[236,473,474],{},"central.api.pilot.*",[236,476,477],{},"central.notification.api.report_pilot_event",", about 28 ",[236,480,481],{},"central.billing.api.billing_api.*",[236,483,484],{},"central.api.email_oauth.*",[236,486,487],{},"central.api.integrations.github.*",[276,489,490,491,494],{},"Header ",[236,492,493],{},"X-Pilot-Token",": 48 hex characters; Central stores only its SHA-256. The team and the server always come from the credential, never from the request",[261,496,497,500,505],{},[276,498,499],{},"Atlas and Cargo",[276,501,502],{},[236,503,504],{},"central.api.state_delivery.receive",[276,506,507,292,510,292,513,516],{},[236,508,509],{},"X-FC-Source",[236,511,512],{},"X-FC-Region",[236,514,515],{},"X-Frappe-Webhook-Signature"," (HMAC-SHA256 with a secret per region and per sender)",[261,518,519,522,527],{},[276,520,521],{},"Anyone",[276,523,524],{},[236,525,526],{},"central.api.jwks.get_jwks",[276,528,529],{},"Nothing: public keys",[261,531,532,535,540],{},[276,533,534],{},"A metered service",[276,536,537],{},[236,538,539],{},"central.billing.api.metering.report",[276,541,542,292,545,548],{},[236,543,544],{},"X-Central-Service",[236,546,547],{},"X-Central-Signature"," (HMAC)",[261,550,551,554,559],{},[276,552,553],{},"Grove",[276,555,556],{},[236,557,558],{},"central.api.grove.datum_token",[276,560,561],{},[236,562,563],{},"X-Grove-Token",[261,565,566,569,572],{},[276,567,568],{},"Payment gateways, GitHub",[276,570,571],{},"Their webhooks",[276,573,574],{},"Their own signatures",[218,576,577,580],{},[241,578,579],{},"Calls."," Atlas, the proxy, the WireGuard gateway and Cargo of each region; Pilot on each server, through the proxy; Datum of one region, for its own errors and gauges; Grove; Stripe, Razorpay, PayPal; GitHub; a Helpdesk site for support tickets. Central is not on the private network of any region and never opens an SSH session to a server.",[218,582,583,586,587,590,591,594],{},[241,584,585],{},"To a customer it gives"," the console: servers (create, start, stop, restart, resize, rename, terminate, rescue mode), firewall rulesets, public addresses, WireGuard devices, SSH keys, a web console, snapshots, \"open bench\" and \"log in to the site as Administrator\", buckets, AI keys, billing, team roles. It gives no API token page and sends no webhook to a customer. An ordinary Frappe API key of a team member does work against ",[236,588,589],{},"central.api.*"," (",[236,592,593],{},"suite_cloud"," relies on it), but nothing in the console issues one.",[228,596,597],{"id":305},"Atlas",[218,599,600,601,604],{},"The virtual machine manager of ",[241,602,603],{},"one region with one provider"," (AWS, Scaleway or generic hardware). A monorepo:",[255,606,607,620],{},[258,608,609],{},[261,610,611,614,617],{},[264,612,613],{},"Part",[264,615,616],{},"What",[264,618,619],{},"Runs",[271,621,622,636,649,664,675],{},[261,623,624,627,633],{},[276,625,626],{},"The Atlas app",[276,628,629,630],{},"Frappe 16 site, REST API under ",[236,631,632],{},"\u002Fapi\u002Fatlas",[276,634,635],{},"One site per region, itself in a virtual machine on a host",[261,637,638,643,646],{},[276,639,640],{},[236,641,642],{},"metald",[276,644,645],{},"Go daemon: Firecracker, ZFS, network namespaces, eBPF",[276,647,648],{},"Every physical host",[261,650,651,656,659],{},[276,652,653],{},[236,654,655],{},"atlas-guest-agent",[276,657,658],{},"Static Go binary",[276,660,661],{},[241,662,663],{},"Inside every virtual machine image",[261,665,666,669,672],{},[276,667,668],{},"The proxy",[276,670,671],{},"OpenResty and a control daemon",[276,673,674],{},"1 to 5 service machines",[261,676,677,680,683],{},[276,678,679],{},"WireGuard mesh, IPv6 router, WireGuard gateway",[276,681,682],{},"eBPF programs and Python",[276,684,685],{},"Hosts and service machines",[218,687,688,690,691,292,693,292,696,292,699,292,702,292,705,292,708,292,711,292,714,717,718,721,722,724,725,292,728,731],{},[241,689,253],{}," ",[236,692,341],{},[236,694,695],{},"Virtual Machine State",[236,697,698],{},"Virtual Machine Image",[236,700,701],{},"Metal Server",[236,703,704],{},"Public IP Pool",[236,706,707],{},"Proxy Server",[236,709,710],{},"Cargo Server",[236,712,713],{},"SSH Task",[236,715,716],{},"Investigation",", and ",[236,719,720],{},"Atlas Settings"," (region id, wildcard domain and certificate, the region's signing key, Central's keys). On each host, ",[236,723,642],{}," keeps the machine's ",[236,726,727],{},"config.json",[236,729,730],{},"status.json"," and 7 days of 10-second samples.",[218,733,734,690,736,739,740,743,744,747,748,751,752,754,755,758,759,762,763,292,766,292,769,292,772,292,775,292,778,292,781,784,785,788,789,292,792,292,795,292,798,292,801,292,804,292,807,292,810,813,814,817],{},[241,735,433],{},[236,737,738],{},"Authorization: Bearer",", an Ed25519 token with audience ",[236,741,742],{},"atlas-admin:\u003Cregion>",", scope ",[236,745,746],{},"*",", a ",[236,749,750],{},"tenant"," claim (",[236,753,746],{}," for Central, a number otherwise) and the header ",[236,756,757],{},"X-Tenant-ID",". Routes: ",[236,760,761],{},"virtual-machines"," and their actions (",[236,764,765],{},"start",[236,767,768],{},"stop",[236,770,771],{},"pause",[236,773,774],{},"resume",[236,776,777],{},"restart",[236,779,780],{},"resize",[236,782,783],{},"snapshot",", rescue mode, ",[236,786,787],{},"console-token","), ",[236,790,791],{},"…\u002Fmetrics",[236,793,794],{},"images",[236,796,797],{},"public-ips",[236,799,800],{},"webhooks",[236,802,803],{},"beacon\u002Fresources",[236,805,806],{},"hosts\u002F\u003Cid>\u002Faccess",[236,808,809],{},"dns-records",[236,811,812],{},"investigations",", and the public ",[236,815,816],{},"jwks.json",". A tenant never holds an Atlas token: Central calls for it. Another tenant's record answers 404.",[218,819,820,690,822,824],{},[241,821,579],{},[236,823,642],{}," on each host (mutual TLS, port 9000, every 10 seconds); Central (the state webhook, and Central's keys every 5 minutes); Cargo (one bucket for its own images); Datum; hosts and service machines over SSH; Route 53; ACME; the hardware's management controllers.",[218,826,827,830],{},[241,828,829],{},"Also in Atlas."," A Warpgate bastion for staff access to hosts (signed in through Central, grants of 24 hours at most); an LLM \"investigator\" with read-only SQL on Datum and SSH to hosts, with no access to customer machines; \"sleepy\" machines that are frozen when no request arrives; rescue mode; live migration.",[228,832,834],{"id":833},"cargo","Cargo",[218,836,837],{},"One Frappe site per region, on a platform machine (tenant 0) that is itself a Pilot bench. Three modules:",[839,840,841,868,878],"ul",{},[842,843,844,847,848,851,852,292,855,292,858,292,861,292,864,867],"li",{},[241,845,846],{},"Image Builder."," It builds Pilot images (Base, Site, Apps) and one-click service images. A build is a virtual machine it rents from Atlas, provisions over SSH, stops, and snapshots. The ",[241,849,850],{},"tags on the snapshot are the hand-over",": ",[236,853,854],{},"purpose=pilot",[236,856,857],{},"pilot_version",[236,859,860],{},"frappe_version",[236,862,863],{},"has_site",[236,865,866],{},"app",". Central finds Pilot images by tag in Atlas; Cargo never tells Central about them.",[842,869,870,873,874,877],{},[241,871,872],{},"Object Storage."," It runs the region's Garage (S3) cluster and creates buckets and keys when Central asks. A bench then speaks S3 to ",[236,875,876],{},"https:\u002F\u002Fs3-svc.\u003Cregion domain>"," directly.",[842,879,880,883,884,887],{},[241,881,882],{},"Telemetry."," It installs and runs the region's ",[241,885,886],{},"Datum and ClickHouse host",", and publishes the key set Datum trusts.",[218,889,890,892,893,896,897,900,901,292,904,907,908,911,912,915,916,919,920,248],{},[241,891,433],{}," Header ",[236,894,895],{},"X-Cargo-Access-Token",": an Ed25519 token with audience ",[236,898,899],{},"atlas-cargo:\u003Cregion>",", signed by Central or by the region's Atlas. Methods: ",[236,902,903],{},"cargo.api.webhooks.configure",[236,905,906],{},"cargo.object_storage.api.bucket.*",", two ",[236,909,910],{},"one_click_image"," methods. Public: ",[236,913,914],{},"cargo.api.jwks.get_jwks",". For its own machines: ",[236,917,918],{},"cargo.api.telemetry.datum_token"," with ",[236,921,922],{},"X-Cargo-Machine-Token",[218,924,925,927,928,930,931,302,934,937],{},[241,926,579],{}," Atlas, as tenant 0, with a token Atlas gave it at install (scope ",[236,929,746],{},", 365 days); Central, with one webhook that says whether ",[236,932,933],{},"storage",[236,935,936],{},"telemetry"," are available and at which address; Datum; its own machines over SSH; GitHub for Pilot's releases and Frappe's branch heads.",[218,939,940],{},"A tenant never talks to Cargo.",[228,942,469],{"id":943},"pilot",[218,945,946,947,950,951,954,955,958,959,962,963,966],{},"\"Frappe Server Manager\", the successor of ",[236,948,949],{},"bench",": a Python CLI, a Flask Admin API (about 300 routes) and a Vue Admin UI. It runs inside each server as one unprivileged user (",[236,952,953],{},"frappe","), in ",[236,956,957],{},"~\u002Fpilot",". It has no database of its own: ",[236,960,961],{},"bench.toml"," per bench, ",[236,964,965],{},"common_config.toml"," per host, task folders, JSON logs.",[218,968,969,970,975,976,248],{},"It is one codebase for two cases. The switch is ",[241,971,972],{},[236,973,974],{},"[central] enabled"," in ",[236,977,965],{},[255,979,980,993],{},[258,981,982],{},[261,983,984,987,990],{},[264,985,986],{},"Behaviour",[264,988,989],{},"Self-hosted",[264,991,992],{},"Frappe Cloud v2",[271,994,995,1005,1023,1033,1046],{},[261,996,997,1000,1003],{},[276,998,999],{},"Benches, sites, apps, Admin UI, tasks, sandbox, nginx, certificates, backups to S3, local metrics, uptime pings, webhooks, mail alerts, the marketplace registry, self-update",[276,1001,1002],{},"Yes",[276,1004,1002],{},[261,1006,1007,1010,1020],{},[276,1008,1009],{},"Telemetry to Datum",[276,1011,1012,1013,302,1016,1019],{},"Only with ",[236,1014,1015],{},"[telemetry] endpoint",[236,1017,1018],{},"token"," set by hand",[276,1021,1022],{},"Token fetched from Central and renewed",[261,1024,1025,1028,1031],{},[276,1026,1027],{},"Alerts to Central, the trial lock, private GitHub repositories through Central, billing in the site's Cloud Settings",[276,1029,1030],{},"No",[276,1032,1002],{},[261,1034,1035,1038,1043],{},[276,1036,1037],{},"Central signs in to the Admin",[276,1039,1012,1040,1019],{},[236,1041,1042],{},"[admin] jwks_url",[276,1044,1045],{},"Set at first boot",[261,1047,1048,1051,1054],{},[276,1049,1050],{},"Routing of a new domain",[276,1052,1053],{},"A DNS check and a local certificate",[276,1055,1056],{},"A program from Cargo's image asks Central",[218,1058,1059,1061,1062,1064,1065,1068,1069,1072],{},[241,1060,433],{}," The Admin API with a session cookie (the bench's Admin password, optional TOTP), a 5-minute token signed by Central (checked against Central's keys and the bench's audience; scope ",[236,1063,949],{},"), or the site's own token (",[236,1066,1067],{},"pilot_auth_token",", HS256, 365 days, scope ",[236,1070,1071],{},"site","). And the machine's metadata service, which is how Central's credential and first settings arrive.",[218,1074,1075,1077,1078,1080,1081,1084,1085,1088,1089,1092],{},[241,1076,579],{}," Central (",[236,1079,493],{},"); Datum; ",[236,1082,1083],{},"github.com\u002Ffrappe\u002Fmarketplace"," (git, at most hourly); ",[236,1086,1087],{},"github.com\u002Ffrappe\u002Fpilot"," releases for its own update (00:00 UTC, on by default, no checksum or signature beyond TLS); the S3 bucket; Let's Encrypt; any ",[236,1090,1091],{},"[[webhook_endpoints]]"," the operator adds.",[218,1094,1095,1096,248],{},"Details of what is on the server and what leaves it: ",[222,1097,205],{"href":206},[228,1099,1101],{"id":1100},"datum","Datum",[218,1103,1104,1105,1108,1109,1112],{},"One FastAPI process per region (two workers on ",[236,1106,1107],{},"127.0.0.1:8000",", behind Caddy), on a host Cargo installs, next to ClickHouse. ",[241,1110,1111],{},"It only writes."," There is no read route.",[255,1114,1115,1125],{},[258,1116,1117],{},[261,1118,1119,1122],{},[264,1120,1121],{},"Route",[264,1123,1124],{},"Body",[271,1126,1127,1140,1150,1160,1170],{},[261,1128,1129,1134],{},[276,1130,1131],{},[236,1132,1133],{},"POST \u002Fv1\u002Fingest",[276,1135,1136,1137],{},"JSON samples ",[236,1138,1139],{},"{metric, value, ts, labels}",[261,1141,1142,1147],{},[276,1143,1144],{},[236,1145,1146],{},"POST \u002Fv1\u002Fingest\u002Fremote",[276,1148,1149],{},"Prometheus remote write v1",[261,1151,1152,1157],{},[276,1153,1154],{},[236,1155,1156],{},"POST \u002Fv1\u002Flogs\u002Fingest",[276,1158,1159],{},"Log lines",[261,1161,1162,1167],{},[276,1163,1164],{},[236,1165,1166],{},"POST \u002Fv1\u002Ftraces",[276,1168,1169],{},"OTLP over HTTP (no application in these repositories sends traces)",[261,1171,1172,1177],{},[276,1173,1174],{},[236,1175,1176],{},"GET \u002Fhealth",[276,1178,1179],{},"Open",[218,1181,1182,1185,1186,747,1189,1192,1193,1196,1197,1200,1201,292,1204,292,1207,1210],{},[241,1183,1184],{},"Authentication."," An Ed25519 token with audience ",[236,1187,1188],{},"atlas-datum:\u003Cregion>",[236,1190,1191],{},"resource_id"," (stamped on every row) and ",[236,1194,1195],{},"access"," containing ",[236,1198,1199],{},"write",". Three issuers are accepted, told apart by the key id's prefix: ",[236,1202,1203],{},"central:",[236,1205,1206],{},"atlas:\u003Cregion>:",[236,1208,1209],{},"cargo:\u003Cregion>:",". Limits: 12 requests per 60 seconds per resource and per route, in each worker; 10,000 samples, lines or spans per request. No queue and no retry on Datum's side.",[218,1212,1213,1216,1217,1219,1220,1223,1224,1227,1228,1231,1232,1235,1236,1239,1240,1243],{},[241,1214,1215],{},"Tables"," (database ",[236,1218,1100],{},"): ",[236,1221,1222],{},"samples"," (15 days for ",[236,1225,1226],{},"system_*",", 90 days otherwise), ",[236,1229,1230],{},"samples_recent"," (2 days), ",[236,1233,1234],{},"samples_5m"," (90 days), ",[236,1237,1238],{},"logs"," (30 days), ",[236,1241,1242],{},"traces"," (7 days), and daily volume statistics.",[218,1245,1246,1249],{},[241,1247,1248],{},"Three addresses",", all served by Caddy on the Datum host:",[255,1251,1252,1265],{},[258,1253,1254],{},[261,1255,1256,1259,1262],{},[264,1257,1258],{},"Address",[264,1260,1261],{},"Goes to",[264,1263,1264],{},"Used by",[271,1266,1267,1279,1292],{},[261,1268,1269,1274,1276],{},[276,1270,1271],{},[236,1272,1273],{},"https:\u002F\u002Ftelemetry-svc.\u003Cregion domain>",[276,1275,1101],{},[276,1277,1278],{},"Senders outside the private network (Central)",[261,1280,1281,1286,1289],{},[276,1282,1283],{},[236,1284,1285],{},"http:\u002F\u002Finternal-telemetry-svc.\u003Cregion domain>",[276,1287,1288],{},"Datum, plain HTTP on the private network",[276,1290,1291],{},"Pilot on customer servers, Cargo's machines. It is the address Cargo reports to Central",[261,1293,1294,1299,1302],{},[276,1295,1296],{},[236,1297,1298],{},"https:\u002F\u002Ftelemetry-read-svc.\u003Cregion domain>",[276,1300,1301],{},"ClickHouse's HTTP interface",[276,1303,1304,1305,1308,1309,306],{},"Beacon (user ",[236,1306,1307],{},"beacon","), Insights (user ",[236,1310,1311],{},"insights",[218,1313,1314,1317,1318,1321,1322,1325],{},[241,1315,1316],{},"The \"Datum agent\""," is Vector 0.59.0 with a fixed configuration, installed as root by Atlas or Cargo on ",[241,1319,1320],{},"hosts, service machines and Cargo's machines",": host metrics, the journal at warning and above, nginx's ",[236,1323,1324],{},"error.log",". It is not installed on customer servers.",[218,1327,1328,1329,1332,1333,1336,1337,1340],{},"The repository has ",[241,1330,1331],{},"no license file",". Three consumers (Pilot's Admin, Cargo, Atlas) import its ",[236,1334,1335],{},"datum_client"," package from the ",[236,1338,1339],{},"main"," branch.",[228,1342,1343],{"id":1307},"Beacon",[218,1345,1346,1347,1349,1350,1353],{},"One Frappe 16 app on ",[241,1348,243],{},", outside the regions it watches. Its home page is the status page. ",[241,1351,1352],{},"It only pulls",": it has no agent and no ingest API.",[218,1355,1356],{},[241,1357,1358],{},"Inputs.",[255,1360,1361,1371],{},[258,1362,1363],{},[261,1364,1365,1368],{},[264,1366,1367],{},"Input",[264,1369,1370],{},"How",[271,1372,1373,1401,1423,1434],{},[261,1374,1375,1378],{},[276,1376,1377],{},"Rules, service levels, charts",[276,1379,1380,1381,292,1384,292,1387,292,1390,292,1393,1396,1397,1400],{},"Files in each producer's repository (",[236,1382,1383],{},"beacon\u002Frules\u002F*.sql",[236,1385,1386],{},"*.http",[236,1388,1389],{},"*.tls",[236,1391,1392],{},"beacon\u002Fservices\u002F*.sql",[236,1394,1395],{},"beacon\u002Fcharts\u002F*.sql","), read through GitHub's API at the head of a branch, ",[241,1398,1399],{},"only when an administrator presses Sync Definitions",". Each new query is run once before anything is saved",[261,1402,1403,1406],{},[276,1404,1405],{},"Telemetry",[276,1407,1408,1409,1411,1412,1415,1416,1419,1420,1422],{},"SQL on each region's ClickHouse, as user ",[236,1410,1307],{}," (read only, 20 seconds, 100,000 rows, ",[236,1413,1414],{},"SELECT"," on ",[236,1417,1418],{},"datum.*","). No row policy exists: ",[236,1421,1307],{}," reads every tenant's rows of the region",[261,1424,1425,1428],{},[276,1426,1427],{},"The resource tree",[276,1429,1430,1433],{},[236,1431,1432],{},"GET \u002Fapi\u002Fatlas\u002Fbeacon\u002Fresources"," on each region's Atlas, every minute: Atlas, the hosts, every virtual machine (customers' included, with its host as parent), the service machines, Cargo",[261,1435,1436,1439],{},[276,1437,1438],{},"HTTP and TLS checks",[276,1440,1441],{},"Made from the Beacon site, every minute, on platform addresses only",[218,1443,1444],{},[241,1445,1446],{},"What the producers declare.",[255,1448,1449,1465],{},[258,1450,1451],{},[261,1452,1453,1456,1459,1462],{},[264,1454,1455],{},"Producer",[264,1457,1458],{},"Rules",[264,1460,1461],{},"Service levels",[264,1463,1464],{},"What they watch",[271,1466,1467,1490,1507,1532],{},[261,1468,1469,1471,1474,1484],{},[276,1470,597],{},[276,1472,1473],{},"36",[276,1475,1476,1477,292,1480,1483],{},"5 (",[236,1478,1479],{},"servers",[236,1481,1482],{},"proxy",", three networking services; 99.9%)",[276,1485,1486,1487,1489],{},"Hosts, ",[236,1488,642],{},", the proxy, the mesh, certificates",[261,1491,1492,1494,1497,1504],{},[276,1493,834],{},[276,1495,1496],{},"21",[276,1498,1499,1500,1503],{},"1 (",[236,1501,1502],{},"object-storage",", 99.9%)",[276,1505,1506],{},"Image builds, Garage, and Datum itself",[261,1508,1509,1511,1514,1529],{},[276,1510,231],{},[276,1512,1513],{},"10",[276,1515,1516,1517,1520,1521,1524,1525,1528],{},"3 (",[236,1518,1519],{},"dashboard-api"," 99.9%, ",[236,1522,1523],{},"server-actions"," 99%, ",[236,1526,1527],{},"billing"," declared)",[276,1530,1531],{},"API errors, payments, stuck actions",[261,1533,1534,1536,1539,1545],{},[276,1535,469],{},[276,1537,1538],{},"5",[276,1540,1499,1541,1544],{},[236,1542,1543],{},"sites"," 99.9%, hidden from the status page)",[276,1546,1547],{},"The only rules that read customer servers' data",[218,1549,1550,1553],{},[241,1551,1552],{},"From alert to person."," Rule → Alert (Pending, Firing, Resolved) → Incident, grouped by the resource tree. Every incident posts to a chat webhook. High and Critical also send email and call the responders through Twilio, one after another (the next after 2 minutes for Critical, 5 for High; a new round every 15 minutes). Answering the call acknowledges. Service levels raise burn alerts over two windows (14.4× over 1 hour and 5 minutes; 6× over 6 hours and 30 minutes; 1× over 3 days and 6 hours, which never pages).",[218,1555,1556,1558],{},[241,1557,585],{}," the public status page, a per-incident RSS feed and email subscription. Nothing else: no account, no API.",[228,1560,1562],{"id":1561},"around-the-six","Around the six",[255,1564,1565,1577],{},[258,1566,1567],{},[261,1568,1569,1572,1574],{},[264,1570,1571],{},"Repository",[264,1573,616],{},[264,1575,1576],{},"Link to the six",[271,1578,1579,1593,1610,1627,1644],{},[261,1580,1581,1587,1590],{},[276,1582,1583,1586],{},[236,1584,1585],{},"cloudtoolkit"," (AGPL-3.0)",[276,1588,1589],{},"Durable pipelines and an SSH client, taken from Press' workflow engine",[276,1591,1592],{},"Only Cargo requires it",[261,1594,1595,1600,1603],{},[276,1596,1597],{},[236,1598,1599],{},"marketplace",[276,1601,1602],{},"The registry of 132 installable apps, one JSON per app",[276,1604,1605,1606,1609],{},"Pilot clones it for ",[236,1607,1608],{},"get-app","; Cargo reads Pilot's copy to choose the apps of a signup image. A new app that passes the automated check merges by itself",[261,1611,1612,1617,1620],{},[276,1613,1614],{},[236,1615,1616],{},"one-click-templates",[276,1618,1619],{},"Redis, MariaDB, Prometheus and Grafana as ready servers",[276,1621,1622,1623,1626],{},"Cargo builds each into an Atlas image; Central writes the customer's answers to ",[236,1624,1625],{},"\u002Fetc\u002Fone-click\u002Finputs.env"," through cloud-init. These servers have no Pilot",[261,1628,1629,1638,1641],{},[276,1630,1631,292,1634,1637],{},[236,1632,1633],{},"grove",[236,1635,1636],{},"pathway"," (MIT)",[276,1639,1640],{},"An AI inference platform: a Frappe control plane and a Go gateway",[276,1642,1643],{},"Central creates teams and keys in Grove, reads usage hourly to bill it, and signs Datum tokens for Grove's machines. Grove's machines come from AWS and RunPod, not from Atlas",[261,1645,1646,1650,1653],{},[276,1647,1648,1586],{},[236,1649,593],{},[276,1651,1652],{},"Mail servers of Frappe Suite",[276,1654,1655],{},"A customer of Central like any other: it creates servers with a team member's API key and drives Pilot. Its mail clusters are outside Frappe Cloud v2",{"title":1657,"searchDepth":1658,"depth":1659,"links":1660},"",1,2,[1661,1662,1663,1664,1665,1666,1667],{"id":230,"depth":1659,"text":231},{"id":305,"depth":1659,"text":597},{"id":833,"depth":1659,"text":834},{"id":943,"depth":1659,"text":469},{"id":1100,"depth":1659,"text":1101},{"id":1307,"depth":1659,"text":1343},{"id":1561,"depth":1659,"text":1562},"Each Frappe Cloud v2 application, what it stores, what it accepts and what it calls.","md",null,{},{"icon":194},{"title":191,"description":1668},"qAbwMaCMBX5xhgIe8AANPDY5W0WtCDGQRwWbhDjd5hg",[1676,1678],{"title":188,"path":184,"stem":185,"description":1677,"icon":189,"children":-1},"What Frappe Cloud v2 is made of, which app owns what, and where the rest of this analysis is.",{"title":196,"path":197,"stem":198,"description":1679,"icon":132,"children":-1},"Every link between two Frappe Cloud v2 applications, with its header, its token and its lifetime.",1795111372941]